'''Ubik Von Neumann''' is an [[NPC]] located in {{Zone|The Mountaintop}} in the [[Rift Dimension]].

== Purpose ==
'''Ubik Von Neumann''' offers the player 3 minigames.

=== Three Options ===
During '''Three Options''', '''Ubik Von Neumann''' asks the player to choose one out of three boxes. After choosing one, they reveal an unchosen box and ask to keep the chosen box or switch. If the correct box was chosen, the player earns an {{ID|IQ Point]}}. The first time the player chooses to switch, '''Ubik Von Neumann''' will ask why. Telling them that it increases the odds of being correct grants an [[Enigma Souls|Enigma Soul]].

=== Averages ===
'''Averages''' lasts for one SkyBlock Year. The player is asked to pick a number from {{Green|1}} to {{Green|100}}. The closest {{Green|10%}} of participants to half of the average obtain a {{Item|Free Will}} and [[Enigma Souls|Enigma Soul]]. Additionally, if a player picks a value at least {{Green|4x}} higher than the average, they earn {{Green|2}} {{Item|Free Will}}s.

If the player fails to win {{Green|5}} times, then '''Ubik Von Neumann''' will grant them the [[Enigma Souls|Enigma Soul]] without a {{Item|Free Will}}.

=== Tit For Tat ===
Each game of '''Tit For Tat''' can last between {{Green|5}} to {{Green|9}} rounds. If both player steal, they earn {{Motes|1000}} each. If both split, they earn {{Motes|3000}}. If one steals and the other splits, the stealer will earn {{Motes|5000}} while the other earns nothing. Upon copying the previous move of '''Ubik Von Neumann''' after choosing SPLIT for the first round, the player earns {{Item|Ubik's Cube}} and an [[Enigma Souls|Enigma Soul]].

