== Trivia ==
* '''Ubik von Neumann''' is likely named after mathematician [[w:John von Neumann|John von Neumann]], a pioneer of [[w:Game theory|game theory]], which directly inspires all three of Ubik's minigames. His first name may also reference the 1969 novel [[w:Ubik|Ubik]] by Philip K. Dick.
** The '''Tit For Tat''' minigame is based on one of the most famous thought experiments in game theory, the [[w:Prisoner's dilemma|Prisoner's dilemma]].
** The '''Three Options''' minigame is based on the probability puzzle known sas the [[w:Monty Hall problem|Monty Hall problem]].
** The '''Averages''' minigame is inspired by the [[w:Keynesian_beauty_contest|Keynesian Beauty Contest]] thought experiment, also known as the [[w:Guess 2/3 of the average|Guess 2/3 of the average]] game.
* Due to the '''Averages''' minigame considering the closest {{Green|10%}} of participants, it is possible to lose despite picking a number that other players won with.
** In case of such a tie, the winners are determined based on unknown criteria (likely their Minecraft account UUID).{{Confirm}}
* 3 NPCs can be seen next to Ubik in the '''Split or Steal''' minigame, who are the rift version of the [[Three Weirdos]].
** Their names are also randomized.
** The red colored NPC is often used for this minigame due to his playstyle being {{Green|100% SPLIT}}, letting players steal every round and get {{Motes|25k|45k}} every game.

